    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0286" n="261" xml:id="pg261"/>

                <head>98. Memorandum by Ambassador at Large Bunker<anchor n="1" xml:id="d98-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1975-09-18">September 18, 1975</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">Clements’ Talks with Senators Byrd and Thurmond </p>
                <p>Steve Low reported that during the past week Deputy Secretary Clements had seen
                    both Senator Byrd and Senator Thurmond.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d98-f2"/> He told
                    them that the negotiations would probably take an extended period of time and
                    did not foresee a treaty being presented to the Senate until after the elections
                    in ’76.</p>
                <p>Both Senator Byrd and Senator Thurmond had responded by saying that in view of
                    the fact that the negotiations would be protracted there was no need for them to
                    press ahead urgently with their views at this time. Clements believed,
                    therefore, that we might see a let-up in the pressure from these sources for the
                    present.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EB<anchor n="3" xml:id="d98-f3"/></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
